@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Nepal MediHub";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] = "About Nepal MediHub - a national health marketplace serving all seven provinces of Nepal, with simulated NID identity and a CEHR-ready integration seam.";
}

<div class="hero-banner mb-5 text-center">
    <i class="bi bi-hospital" style="font-size: 4rem; color: var(--primary-teal);"></i>
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mt-3 mb-2" style="color: var(--primary-teal);">About Nepal MediHub</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted mb-0">A national health marketplace, built as course work for CSC381</p>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3" style="color: var(--primary-teal);">Our Mission</h2>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">Nepal MediHub is a BSc CSIT final-year project that sets out to make medicines and health supplies reachable to people across the whole country, not only in the capital. It is an online-only platform: there is no physical store, and orders are delivered to the customer's address in any district.</p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">The project also explores what a citizen-centred health platform could look like. Each account is tied to a simulated National ID, and the codebase keeps a clean seam for a future centralized electronic health record. A customer can review their own purchase history in one place, which is the sort of feature a national record system would eventually build on.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm text-center h-100 p-4">
                    <i class="bi bi-shield-fill-check" style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--success-green);"></i>
                    <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2">Nationwide Reach</h5>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">Checkout covers all seven provinces and their districts, from the Terai plains up to the high Himalaya.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm text-center h-100 p-4">
                    <i class="bi bi-truck" style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--accent-blue);"></i>
                    <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2">Online-Only</h5>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">No walk-in counter. Everything from browsing to payment happens on the site.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm text-center h-100 p-4">
                    <i class="bi bi-credit-card-2-front" style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--primary-teal);"></i>
                    <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2">Sandbox Payments</h5>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">Checkout runs against the eSewa test environment, with cash on delivery also available.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 mb-4" style="background-color: #f0fdfa;">
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3" style="color: var(--primary-teal);">Simulated National ID</h2>
            <p class="text-muted">Registration asks for a National ID, but it is a simulation built entirely inside this project. The number is checked for format and uniqueness against our own database and nothing else. No request ever leaves the server, and no real citizen record is consulted or created.</p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">Keeping the identity layer separate from the shop layer was deliberate. Swapping the local check for a call to a real national identity service would only mean reimplementing one method on the identity service, without touching the controllers or views.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3" style="color: var(--primary-teal);">Product Categories We Serve</h2>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <ul class="list-unstyled">
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>Prescription Medicines</strong> - Antibiotics, chronic disease medications (upload a prescription)</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>OTC Medicines</strong> - Pain relief, cold &amp; flu, digestive health, allergy relief</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>Vitamins &amp; Supplements</strong> - Multivitamins, calcium, omega-3, protein powders</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <ul class="list-unstyled">
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>Medical Equipment</strong> - Blood pressure monitors, glucometers, thermometers, nebulizers</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>First Aid &amp; Wound Care</strong> - Bandages, antiseptics, gauze, medical tape</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2" style="color: var(--success-green);"></i><strong>Health &amp; Wellness</strong> - Personal care, mother &amp; baby care, diabetic care</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-danger border-0 shadow-sm" role="alert">
    <h6 class="alert-heading"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill me-2"></i>Medical Disclaimer</h6>
    <p class="small mb-2">Nepal MediHub sells medicines and health products for information and purchase purposes only. It is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis or treatment, and no prescription uploaded here is legally validated.</p>
    <ul class="small mb-2">
        <li>Always seek the advice of your physician or qualified healthcare provider with any questions regarding a medical condition.</li>
        <li>Never disregard professional medical advice or delay seeking it because of information on this website.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small fw-bold mb-0"><i class="bi bi-telephone-fill me-2"></i>For medical emergencies, call 102 (National Ambulance Service) or 103 (Nepal Police Emergency).</p>
</div>
